<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefan Crnojević</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1465</span> · Also known as Stefanica Crnojević</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefan Crnojević was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> from about 1451 to 1465 and the founder of the Crnojević state's power in the Montenegrin highlands. An ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, whose sister Mara he married, he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a> and held the mountain districts against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and the Serbian Despotate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-crnojevic.jpg" alt="Stefan Crnojević" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Varri_i_Mara_Kastrioti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
